mission "The Governor's Ledger"
    name "The Governor's Ledger"
    description "Travel from Tortuga to Port Royal and obtain the ledger page that exposes the governor's secret dealings with Captain Vane."
    source "Port Azure"
    destination "Port Royal"
    lead "Don Rafael slides a folded note across the table. “A factor in Port Azure knows where these duplicate books were printed. His name is Amaro Velez. He has been asking after anyone who can keep a confidence. No need to rush there tonight; the islands are full of work between here and there.”"
    reward 420
    speaker offer "Don Rafael, Captain of the Watch"
    speaker visit "Nell the Chandlery Keeper"
    speaker complete "Nell the Chandlery Keeper"
    to offer
        has "Clear the Cutlass Shoals: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Don Rafael waits beside the harbour guns after sunset. The lantern light catches the silver braid on his coat, but his face is drawn and tired.`
            `"You have done more for this coast than the governor's whole fleet. There is something I need you to see. A clerk stole a page from the governor's private ledger. It records payments to Captain Vane, made before the attacks began."`
            `"The clerk is hiding in Port Royal. Her name is Nell. Take this seal to her. She will know you come from me."`
            choice
                `"Why would the governor pay a pirate?"`
                    goto truth
                `"Give me the seal. I'll find this clerk."`
                    goto accept_job
                `"I won't meddle in a governor's affairs."`
                    goto decline_job
            label truth
                `Rafael looks toward the governor's palace. "Vane was given patrol routes, convoy dates, and the names of ships carrying silver. The governor calls it intelligence work. I call it treason."`
                choice
                    `"I'll get the ledger page to Port Royal."`
                        goto accept_job
                    `"That sounds like a quick way to hang. No."`
                        goto decline_job
            label accept_job
                `Rafael presses a small brass seal into your palm. "Find Nell at the chandlery near the western quay. Bring back the truth, not another rumour."`
                accept
            label decline_job
                `Rafael puts the seal away. "I cannot blame you. Some truths cost more than gold."`
                close
    on accept
        log "Don Rafael has sent you to Port Royal to find Nell and obtain a page from the governor's ledger."
    on visit
        conversation
            `The chandlery smells of tar, rope, and hot wax. A woman with a pistol tucked into her apron studies Rafael's seal before she lets you inside.`
            `"Nell, if you please. That ledger page is real. I copied it before the governor's men burned the book. Vane was paid to leave certain ships alone and sink the rest."`
            `She folds a water-stained page into oilskin. "Take this to Marta at Tortuga. She knows how to make a secret travel farther than a cannon shot."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Nell watches you hide the page beneath your coat. "There. Now the governor cannot pretend the ink is a sailor's invention. Marta at Tortuga will know what to do with it."`
            `She gives you a small purse. "And captain? Do not trust any ship flying clean colours. Some of the dirtiest work is done under a royal flag."`
        log "Found the ledger evidence in Port Royal. The governor has been secretly supplying Captain Vane."
